***Disclaimer:** I am an AI, not a CPA or tax professional. The following is for informational purposes to help you prepare, but you should consult a tax professional or use certified tax software to ensure accuracy.*

### 1. Income & How to Report It
*   **W-2 Income ($79,400):** Reported on Form 1040, Line 1.
*   **Freelance Web Design ($15,000):** This

  Chunk 6/13 (512 chars):
  is self-employment income. You will report this on **Schedule C**. You will also need to pay self-employment tax (Medicare and Social Security) on your net profit using **Schedule SE**.
*   **Interest Income ($2,040 total):** Because your combined interest from Discover ($1,560) and Fidelity ($480) exceeds $1,500, you are required to file **Schedule B**.

### 2. Home Office Deduction
Since you have a dedicated space used *exclusively* for your freelance business, you can deduct a portion of your rent and ut

  Chunk 7/13 (511 chars):
  ilities against your $15,000 freelance income. This goes on your Schedule C and lowers your self-employment tax. You have two options:
*   **Simplified Method:** 165 sq ft × $5/sq ft = **$825 deduction**.
*   **Actual Expenses Method:** Your office is 23.91% of your home (165 / 690 sq ft). Your annual rent is $20,640 ($1,720 × 12). 23.91% of your rent is **$4,935**. You can also deduct 23.91% of your renter's insurance and utilities (electricity, internet). 
*   **Verdict:** The Actual Expenses method will

  Chunk 8/13 (512 chars):
